    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224-a3">

                <pb facs="0487" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg417"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 531.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                            Piatt.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-04-11"><hi rendition="#small-caps">April</hi> 11,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the reception of your
                    letter of the 7th, containing a full and satisfactory report upon the case of
                    Edmund O’ B. Kennedy, <hi rendition="#italic">alias</hi> Featherstone. I fully
                    approve of your action in this matter.</p>
                <p>In the absence of documentary evidence of his citizenship, and his insufficient
                    explanation of certain suspicious circumstances, I do not think it my duty to
                    intervene except under instructions from the Department of State.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
